When going back the next day, my Wordpress would not open.  Turns out this was an issue with permissions that required me going into the Directory -
  sudo nano /etc/apache2/apache2.conf
And adding Directory -
<Directory /var/www/>
    Options Indexes FollowSymLinks
    AllowOverride None
    Require all granted
</Directory>

The previous day I had also tried to fix the issue of changing IPs every time I closed my VM. I had ran SELECT * FROM wp_options WHERE option_name IN('siteurl','home'); in mysql to make the IP what it was at the time I tried to fix this.
Unfortunately, this just meant that when I closed the VM again I was unable to open Wordpress.
I ran the SELECT command again and updated with my current IP:
> UPDATE wp_options
    -> SET option_value = 'http://IP/wordpress'
    -> WHERE option_name = 'siteurl';
 UPDATE wp_options
    -> SET option_value = 'http://IP/'
    -> WHERE option_name = 'home';

This resolved my issues, but it does mean that I need to keep my VM running constantly so the IP doesn't change.
